[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: the parser reads dates month first. Read
the reports and they describe three problems. We merged on subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), so nobody read the bodies, and the
problems ended up in one ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one fix. The parser fix leaves the other two problems open.
</Callout>

## The three problems

1. **parser:** the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
   so a booking for 7 April lands on 4 July.
   [Issue #1](https://github.com/KamilBielarczyk/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)
2. **hint:** the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. A day-first tenant's
   people type the month first, as the hint tells them, and the form reads the day first.
   The parser fix does not touch this.
   [Issue #2](https://github.com/KamilBielarczyk/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)
3. **one-day move:** some bookings move by one day, not by a swapped month. "Client in Lisbon
   got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." No day/month swap explains these.
   [Issue #3](https://github.com/KamilBielarczyk/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3)

## Counts

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

The table sorts reports by tenant: where they are and which booking form they run. Intake's tag
is a guess from the browser, and it disagrees with the tenant often. The one-day moves are the
reports the desk read as a one-day move; they come out of the cause their tenant files them
under.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## What to do with new reports

- Month and day swapped, booking-v3 form: issue #2. Any other way in: issue #1.
- One day off, or different days for people in different places: issue #3.
- Same subject line is not the same problem. Read the body before you merge.

